"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and MS disclose that credit ratings influence the cost and availability of financing and specifically highlight the impact on trading revenues in businesses where counterparty creditworthiness is critical, such as OTC derivatives. BAC specifies that a reduction 'may have a material adverse effect... on certain revenues, particularly in those businesses where counterparty creditworthiness is critical,' while MS states ratings 'can have an impact on certain trading revenues, particularly in those businesses where longer-term counterparty performance is a key consideration.' Both link rating risk directly to specific trading business lines.",
